      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is entirely realistic to give up when the weight of existence feels absolute, and there is no point in forcing a narrative where a character who has exhausted all hope finds a sudden, miraculous spark. The only way to make this feel true is to let Elias's silence be the final answer, where the act of writing becomes a way to acknowledge that the loop has no exit. You don't need to rescue him; you just need to let the story reflect the terrifying, quiet truth that sometimes the only way forward is to stop trying to move at all.",
